    "turn_text": "Well, good morning to you, Brad. And yeah, this is an important move for the region. And I want to commend Mayor Brownin and Mayor Leclerc and Of course, Senator Blumenthal and Murphy for their efforts as well. But as you know, Brad, we've had both Bill Schuster, the Republican, and Peter Defazio, the Democrat up here, because as we often say on your program, you know, infrastructure is neither Democrat or Republican, it's American, and it's absolutely what we needed. And these levy systems have been under siege, you might say, and haven't really had any major repairs for close to 70 years, and so this is a vital step forward. In order to move forward, the Army Corps has to make sure that this first expedited step takes place to evaluate what's called undersea bitch or others called sand piping, which is actually eroding our levy system from underneath, which would place us, the Hartford and East Hartford, in a very catastrophic situation.",
