    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, it all depends on the evaluation of the study. That's why we've called for an expedited study It's also Brad as you know why we proposed tunneling as well because the Army Corps has identified that a lot of the problems that have created the stress on this levy system is from the I-84-91 interchange that goes right over the Buckley Bridge, which has been, on both sides of the risk, has been identified with a lot of the under seepage problems that we're going to have to deal with. So we would hope, and of course, that this would be certainly earmarked in a way that because of its urgency and the catastrophic nature that could occur, that we're able to move this up in terms of the urgency. This is the I-84 interchange and 91 interchange is the number one clock point for the state of Connecticut, number two for New England, and number 24 in the nation. And then when you add to that, the urgency as it relates to under seat-bitch, we think we've got a strong case to be made for for the federal government to expedite this process, especially as it relates to the levies.",
